{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013a74muASTTgKMt6g6WQyUC","type":"tool_result","content":"{\n \"gate\": \"G2\",\n \"title\": \"Credential lifetime and handling\",\n \"lead_role\": \"infrastructure\",\n \"requirement\": \"Issue short-lived credentials from a managed identity or secrets service. Keep long-lived secrets out of prompts, images, and checked-in config. Where the service supports it, bind tokens to their holder (mTLS, DPoP, or workload proof tokens). Then a copied token won't work from another machine. Don't use fixed API keys when short-lived or federated credentials are available. Show that credentials expire and rotate, and explain why you chose their lifetime.\",\n \"not_covered\": [\n  {\n   \"problem\": \"A credential scoped to more operations, resources, or tenants than needed\",\n   \"owner\": \"B02\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"problem\": \"No way to cut off the agent's access without cutting off the user\",\n   \"owner\": \"B04\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"problem\": \"Secrets showing up in tool output, responses, or normal logs\",\n   \"owner\": \"R03\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"problem\": \"Container image not pinned by digest or signature-checked\",\n   \"owner\": \"B10\"\n  }\n ],\n \"na_when\": \"never\",\n \"checks\": [\n  {\n   \"id\": \"B03.1\",\n   \"check\": \"Credentials are fetched at run time from a managed identity or secrets service, not fixed API keys, where short-lived or federated credentials are available.\",\n   \"verify\": \"1) Find credential setup (`AssumeRole`, IRSA, Workload Identity, Managed Identity, Vault, `os.environ`, `process.env`). 2) Check each credential is fetched at run time. 3) Answer no if a fixed key (`AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID`, `API_K\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Write one answer into a findings file, check it, and show what's next.\n\nUse this instead of editing the JSON by hand.\n\n  Answer a check:\n    python answer.py FINDINGS.json check B05.2 --met no --evidence src/x.py:41 \\\\\n        --quote \"exact code on that line\" --note \"what the code does\" [--counter \"what you searched\"]\n\n  Add a red flag:\n    python answer.py FINDINGS.json flag B05 --evidence src/x.py:41 --note \"what's wrong\"\n\n  Finish an item:\n    python answer.py FINDINGS.json item B05 --rating gap --confidence high \\\\\n        --summary \"one sentence\" --next \"what to fix\" [--violates \"exact words from the requirement\"] \\\\\n        [--also-affects E06]\n\n  Resolve a pre-scan hit:\n    python answer.py FINDINGS.json prescan H003 --verdict confirmed --item R03 --reason \"...\"\n\n  Show the next unanswered check:\n    python answer.py FINDINGS.json next\n\nThe quote is checked against the file right away; a \"yes\" without a matching quote\nand a counter-search is refused. Paths are relative to the repo, which defaults to the\nfolder holding FINDINGS.json (set --repo to change it).\n\"\"\"\nimport argparse\nimport json\nimport sys\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nsys.path.insert(0, str(Path(__file__).resolve().parent))\nfrom validate_findings import quote_found, norm, refs  # noqa: E402\n\nCHECKS_FILE = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent / \"references\" / \"checks.json\"\n\n\ndef load(path):\n    return json.loads(Path(path).read_text())\n\n\ndef save(path, doc):\n    Path(path).write_text(json.dumps(doc, indent=2) + \"\\n\")\n\n\ndef find_item(doc, item):\n    for f in doc[\"findings\"]:\n        if f[\"item\"] == item:\n            return f\n    sys.exit(f\"{item} isn't in this findings file.\")\n\n\ndef next_open(doc):\n    for f in doc[\"findings\"]:\n        for c in f.get(\"checks\", []):\n            if c.get(\"met\") == \"unknown\" and not norm(c.get(\"note\", \"\")):\n                return f\"Next: {c['id']} — {c.get('check', '')}\\n  How to verify: {c.get('verify', '')}\"\n        if str(f.get(\"summary\", \"\")).startswith(\"TODO\"):\n            return f\"Next: finish item {f['item']} with `answer.py ... item {f['item']} --rating ...`\"","is_error":false}]},