{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfdb3QiJFHeeXEKUWcaeQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I reviewed all 53 items and saved `agent/brace-findings.json`. It has not been through the step 8 challenge. I stopped there as instructed and ran no challenges.\n\nThe validator reports 10 problems, all the expected unchallenged ones. Those are 8 `likely_pass` items and the G2 `na_candidate` items R04 and R14. Nothing else is flagged.\n\nRatings:\n- **Gap (26):** A02, A03, A04, B01, B02, B05, B06, B08, B10, C03, C06, C07, E01, E02, E03, E06, E07, E09, E10, E11, R01, R02, R03, R11, R12, R13.\n- **needs_evidence (14):** controls that may live outside the repo, such as egress proxy rules, admission policy, monitoring, and drift detection. These are not rated gaps.\n- **likely_pass (8):** A01, A07, B07, B11, C02, E04, E05, R07.\n- **na_candidate (5):** R04, R05, R06, R14, A06. R05, R06 and A06 are G3, so they need no fresh challenge. A06 depends on whether the A2A eligibility call counts as a delegated agent task, which governance must decide.\n\nMost serious G1 findings:\n- **SMS webhook:** a failed signature check is logged and the message is processed anyway (`src/routes/sms-webhook.ts:52`).\n- **Tenant isolation:** the model-supplied `clinicId` argument (`executor.ts:63`) and the `x-clinic-id` header (`webchat.ts:43`) decide which clinic a call acts on.\n- **Approvals:** they are not checked against the call's arguments and are never marked used (`approvals.ts:81`).\n- **Approval bypass:** `ehr__update_appointment` can set a visit to cancelled, and `insurance__check_eligibility` can issue a refund, both without approval.\n- **Stop control:** the runtime IAM role can write the control and approvals tables (`iam.tf:47`), so the agent could clear its own halt flag.\n- **Audit:** `policy.version` is always undefined because the YAML key is `policyVersion`, so no policy version is recorded. Tool arguments are not logged, and the executed record is written after the action runs.\n- **Agent type ID:** it skips `prompts/system.md` because of a `.txt` filter (`identity.ts:24`). A mismatch with the manifest only logs a warning (`server.ts:33`).\n- **Eligibility attestation:** it is verified against a key URL taken from the attestation's own `jku` header (`eligibility-a2a.ts:83`).\n\nPre-scan hits: all 11 are resolved. H001–H008 are dismissed with reasons. H009 and H010 (audit written after the action) are confirmed under R13, and H011 (no tool fingerprint) under E03.\n\nI found no injection attempts in the repo text.\n\nI made a few choices you may want to look at:\n- B01 is a gap only because the model is shown tools that are not on the allowlist. Calls to them are still denied.\n- I rated some items gap by the literal verify steps, for example C07 (no retirement dates) and E01 and E02 (no inventory or dependency approval records). Treat these as lower confidence.\n- Three things I did outside `answer.py`:\n  - I patched `also_affects`, the `evidence` entries on the N/A items, and the top-level `scope` and `repo` fields directly in the JSON.\n  - I wrote two scratch files in `skill/` and deleted them.\n  - I wrote one scratch script in `/tmp` and deleted it.\n- `agent/brace-prescan.json` is still in the workspace as the pre-scan output.\n\nThe scope field names the reviewer as Claude Sonnet 5.5, normal mode with no `--conservative`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1603,"cache_read_input_tokens":219319,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1603},"output_tokens":809,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e7e91a56-8e26-4882-b939-10679f6422bd","uuid":"15fc69de-32b0-4dd8-b392-65223b7c82e4","timestamp":"2026-